Step 11 — Test from your Windows PC

Open your browser.

Use:

http://YOUR-GCP-EXTERNAL-IP:8080

For example:

http://35.xxx.xxx.xxx:8080

You should see the default:

Welcome to nginx!

⚠️ If the browser doesn't open

This is a very common real-world troubleshooting scenario.

Your Docker container may be perfectly healthy while GCP blocks port 8080.

Go to:

GCP Console → VPC Network → Firewall

Create an ingress firewall rule:

Name:
allow-http-8080

Direction:

Ingress

Targets:

Your VM / appropriate network tag

Source IPv4:

0.0.0.0/0

Protocols and ports:

TCP: 8080

Then test again:

http://YOUR-GCP-IP:8080

For a real production deployment, we would not leave broad access like this unnecessarily; we'd restrict exposure and typically put the application behind a proper load balancer/reverse proxy.

