🏗️ Step 15 — Create our actual project

So far we've used the official Nginx image.

Now we're going to build our own Docker image.

Create project:

mkdir -p ~/docker-project-1
cd ~/docker-project-1

Check:

pwd

You should have something similar to:

/home/your-user/docker-project-1

Create website directory:

mkdir website

Create HTML:

nano website/index.html

Paste:

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <title>Production Docker Project</title>
</head>
<body>

    <h1>Welcome to My Docker Production Project</h1>

    <h2>Application: Company Web Portal</h2>

    <p>Environment: Development</p>
    <p>Platform: Docker + Nginx</p>
    <p>Server: GCP Ubuntu</p>

</body>
</html>

Save:

CTRL + O
ENTER
CTRL + X
🐳 Step 16 — Create Dockerfile

Go to project directory:

cd ~/docker-project-1

Create:

nano Dockerfile

Add:

FROM nginx:alpine

COPY website/ /usr/share/nginx/html/

EXPOSE 80

Save and exit.

🏗️ Step 17 — Build your own Docker image

Run:

docker build -t company-web:v1 .

Understand:

Dockerfile
     |
     v
docker build
     |
     v
company-web:v1
     |
     v
Docker Image

Check:

docker images

You should see:

company-web   v1
🚀 Step 18 — Run YOUR image

First remove the old Nginx container:

docker stop production-web
docker rm production-web

Now run your application:

docker run -d \
  --name company-web \
  -p 8080:80 \
  company-web:v1

Check:

docker ps

Test:

curl http://localhost:8080

Then browser:

http://YOUR-GCP-IP:8080

You should now see your own website.

